mpvpaper: draw at the output's own pixels on a fractionally scaled output

mpvpaper only reads wl_output's integer scale, so on a 1.6 output it drew at
2× (3600×2250 on a 2880×1800 panel): mpv scaled the video up to that and the
compositor scaled it down again, two resamplings that soften the picture and
draw 56% more pixels. With wp_fractional_scale_v1 and wp_viewporter (when the
compositor has both), the buffer is the output's size in pixels (logical ×
preferred scale) and the viewport maps it onto the logical size: shown 1:1.
Upstream: https://github.com/GhostNaN/mpvpaper (no fractional scaling yet).

